//! The partner market (genetics specification 11.2, ADR-0018 sections 1 and 2): each month
//! the single women of 16 or more may search; in the order of their rank each chooses
//! among up to twelve single men of 16 or more, by rank, relatives with `φ ≥ 1/8`
//! skipped, the one with the largest utility (the age gap, the kinship penalty and Gumbel
//! noise); a man chosen earlier in the round is taken, and she gets nobody.
//!
//! The expected bytes and stories come from `tools/state_reference.py`, which runs the
//! model of `tools/world_reference.py`, written from the design note of the market and not
//! from this code.
//!
//! Scenario "market": seed 0xff, founder tag `test:market`, the repository's data with the
//! search height `c` = 1.0 (so that rounds have several searchers), forty years. Three
//! couples (20 and 24, 21 and 25, 22 and 23 years old), two single women (20, 21) and two
//! single men (25, 40). In round 1 both women choose sim 9: sim 8 gets him, sim 7 nobody;
//! in round 2 she pairs with the man of 40. Later, a girl of 17 skips her twin brother
//! (round 238), a girl of 17 has her cousin in her list (round 478), and a boy is a
//! candidate from his 16th birthday on (round 502).

